      "displayName": "A. Soroka",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A24c578cc-15e9-4649-9f68-5eace85735e0",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Nothing wrong with using the <tt>EventBus</tt> in those modules in which it should be visible (just kernel-modeshape, I think) but otherwise, (e.g. in http-api) I don't think we should assume its existence. In that case, a strong alternative is to use Awaitility features with <tt>AtomicBoolean</tt> flags, or <tt>Semaphore</tt> instances, or other <tt>java.util.concurrent</tt> or <tt>java.util.concurrent.atomic</tt> features.</p>",
     "created": "29/Sep/16 10:31 AM",
     "id": "17676",
     "jsdPublic": true,
